   "source": [
    "# NOTEBOOK 11 — CAREER READINESS\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project\n",
    "Job Market Analyzer for Career Readiness in South Africa\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate a transparent Career Readiness Score that answers: How prepared is this candidate for the selected career?\n",
    "\n",
    "## Position in Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Previous: Notebook 10 — Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Current: Notebook 11\n",
    "\n",
    "Next: Notebook 12 — Job Market Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "## Main Objective\n",
    "Calculate career readiness by combining skill readiness, experience readiness, education readiness, certification readiness, project readiness, and market alignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Input\n",
    "- `data/processed/sa_it_jobs_matched.csv` — matched job dataset\n",
    "- `data/processed/candidate_profile.json` — candidate profile\n",
    "\n",
    "## Output\n",
    "- Career Readiness Score (0-100)\n",
    "- Component breakdown\n",
    "- Strengths and gaps identification\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTEBOOK ROADMAP\n",
    "\n",
    "STEP 1 — Define Career Readiness\n",
    "STEP 2 — Define Readiness Components\n",
    "STEP 3 — Calculate Skill Readiness\n",
    "STEP 4 — Calculate Experience Readiness\n",
    "STEP 5 — Calculate Education Readiness\n",
    "STEP 6 — Calculate Certification Readiness\n",
    "STEP 7 — Calculate Project Readiness\n",
    "STEP 8 — Calculate Market Alignment\n",
    "STEP 9 — Combine Components\n",
    "STEP 10 — Calculate Final Readiness Score\n",
    "STEP 11 — Interpret the Score\n",
    "STEP 12 — Identify Strengths\n",
    "STEP 13 — Identify Gaps\n",
    "STEP 14 — Validate Results\n",
    "STEP 15 — Save Career Readiness Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 1 — Define Career Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Establish what career readiness means for this project.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Definition\n",
    "Career Readiness is a holistic measure of how prepared a candidate is for their target career, considering skills, education, experience, certifications, projects, and market alignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Career Readiness = 0.40 × Skill Readiness + 0.20 × Experience Readiness + 0.15 × Education Readiness + 0.10 × Certification Readiness + 0.10 × Project Readiness + 0.05 × Market Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate each component separately, then combine with weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 2 — Define Readiness Components\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Document all components of career readiness.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Components\n",
    "| Component | Weight | Description |\n",
    "|-----------|--------|-------------|\n",
    "| Skill Readiness | 40% | How well candidate skills match job requirements |\n",
    "| Experience Readiness | 20% | How well candidate experience matches requirements |\n",
    "| Education Readiness | 15% | How well candidate education matches requirements |\n",
    "| Certification Readiness | 10% | Relevant certifications held |\n",
    "| Project Readiness | 10% | Relevant projects completed |\n",
    "| Market Alignment | 5% | Alignment with job market trends |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate each component on a 0-100 scale."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 3 — Calculate Skill Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate how well the candidate's skills match the job market requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Compare candidate skills with the most demanded skills in the job market.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Skill Readiness = (Number of demanded skills possessed / Total demanded skills) × 100"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load data\n",
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('data/processed/candidate_profile.json', 'r') as f:\n",
    "    candidate = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('data/processed/sa_it_jobs_matched.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract all demanded skills\n",
    "all_skills = []\n",
    "for skills in df['Skills'].dropna():\n",
    "    all_skills.extend([s.strip().lower() for s in str(skills).split(',')])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get top 20 most demanded skills\n",
    "skill_demand = pd.Series(all_skills).value_counts().head(20)\n",
    "demanded_skills = set(skill_demand.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Candidate skills\n",
    "candidate_skills = set(s.lower() for s in candidate['skills'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate skill readiness\n",
    "matched_demanded = demanded_skills & candidate_skills\n",
    "skill_readiness = (len(matched_demanded) / len(demanded_skills)) * 100 if demanded_skills else 0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Skill Readiness:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Demanded skills (top 20): {len(demanded_skills)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate skills: {len(candidate_skills)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Matched demanded skills: {len(matched_demanded)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Skill Readiness: {skill_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 4 — Calculate Experience Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate how well the candidate's experience matches the job market.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Compare candidate experience with typical experience requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Experience Readiness = min(Candidate Experience / Average Required Experience, 1) × 100"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate experience readiness\n",
    "candidate_experience = 0  # Entry-level candidate\n",
    "avg_required_experience = df['Experience_Years'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "experience_readiness = min(candidate_experience / avg_required_experience, 1) * 100 if avg_required_experience > 0 else 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Experience Readiness:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate experience: {candidate_experience} years\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average required experience: {avg_required_experience:.1f} years\")\n",
    "print(f\"Experience Readiness: {experience_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 5 — Calculate Education Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate how well the candidate's education matches the job market.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Compare candidate education level with typical requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Education Readiness = (Candidate Education Level / Average Required Level) × 100"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate education readiness\n",
    "candidate_education_level = 5  # Bachelor's degree\n",
    "avg_required_education = df['education_level'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "education_readiness = min(candidate_education_level / avg_required_education, 1) * 100 if avg_required_education > 0 else 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Education Readiness:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate education level: {candidate_education_level} (Bachelor's)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average required education level: {avg_required_education:.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Education Readiness: {education_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 6 — Calculate Certification Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose",
    "Calculate the candidate's certification readiness.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Count relevant certifications held by the candidate.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Certification Readiness = min(Number of Relevant Certifications / 3, 1) × 100"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate certification readiness\n",
    "candidate_certs = candidate.get('certifications', [])\n",
    "num_certs = len(candidate_certs)\n",
    "\n",
    "certification_readiness = min(num_certs / 3, 1) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Certification Readiness:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate certifications: {num_certs}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Certifications: {candidate_certs}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Certification Readiness: {certification_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 7 — Calculate Project Readiness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate the candidate's project readiness.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Count relevant projects completed by the candidate.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Project Readiness = min(Number of Relevant Projects / 2, 1) × 100"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate project readiness\n",
    "candidate_projects = candidate.get('projects', [])\n",
    "num_projects = len(candidate_projects)\n",
    "\n",
    "project_readiness = min(num_projects / 2, 1) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Project Readiness:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate projects: {num_projects}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Project Readiness: {project_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 8 — Calculate Market Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate how well the candidate aligns with the job market.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Use the average match score from the matching analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Market Alignment = Average Match Score"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate market alignment\n",
    "market_alignment = df['match_score'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Market Alignment:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"Average match score: {market_alignment:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 9 — Combine Components\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Combine all readiness components with weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Weights\n",
    "- Skill Readiness: 40%\n",
    "- Experience Readiness: 20%\n",
    "- Education Readiness: 15%\n",
    "- Certification Readiness: 10%\n",
    "- Project Readiness: 10%\n",
    "- Market Alignment: 5%\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate weighted sum."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Combine components\n",
    "weights = {\n",
    "    'skill_readiness': 0.40,\n",
    "    'experience_readiness': 0.20,\n",
    "    'education_readiness': 0.15,\n",
    "    'certification_readiness': 0.10,\n",
    "    'project_readiness': 0.10,\n",
    "    'market_alignment': 0.05\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "components = {\n",
    "    'skill_readiness': skill_readiness,\n",
    "    'experience_readiness': experience_readiness,\n",
    "    'education_readiness': education_readiness,\n",
    "    'certification_readiness': certification_readiness,\n",
    "    'project_readiness': project_readiness,\n",
    "    'market_alignment': market_alignment\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "career_readiness = sum(components[k] * weights[k] for k in weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Career Readiness Components:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "for component, score in components.items():\n",
    "    weight = weights[component]\n",
    "    weighted = score * weight\n",
    "    print(f\"  {component:25s}: {score:5.1f}% × {weight:.2f} = {weighted:5.2f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Career Readiness Score: {career_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 10 — Calculate Final Readiness Score\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Display the final career readiness score.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "The final score is already calculated in STEP 9."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Final score visualization\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "components_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Component': list(components.keys()),\n",
    "    'Score': list(components.values()),\n",
    "    'Weight': list(weights.values())\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "colors = ['#FF6B6B', '#4ECDC4', '#45B7D1', '#96CEB4', '#FFEAA7', '#DDA0DD']\n",
    "plt.barh(components_df['Component'], components_df['Score'], color=colors)\n",
    "plt.title('Career Readiness Components', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Score (0-100)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Component')\n",
    "plt.xlim(0, 100)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('outputs/career_readiness_components.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFinal Career Readiness Score: {career_readiness:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 11 — Interpret the Score\n",
    "\n",
    "## Result Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "### What happened?\n",
    "Career readiness was calculated by combining six components with weighted importance.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What does it mean?\n",
    "The score indicates how prepared the candidate is for their target career.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why does it matter?\n",
    "Career readiness provides a holistic view of candidate preparedness.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What decision does it support?\n",
    "The score helps identify areas for improvement.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What limitation should be considered?\n",
    "The weights are design choices and may not be optimal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 12 — Identify Strengths\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Identify the candidate's strengths.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Find components with high scores."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify strengths\n",
    "strengths = [name for name, score in components.items() if score >= 70]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Candidate Strengths:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "for strength in strengths:\n",
    "    print(f"  - {strength}: {components[strength]:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 13 — Identify Gaps\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Identify the candidate's gaps.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Find components with low scores."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify gaps\n",
    "gaps = [name for name, score in components.items() if score < 50]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Candidate Gaps:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "for gap in gaps:\n",
    "    print(f\"  - {gap}: {components[gap]:.1f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
